{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfRi7vLeb47guZeBszECW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JLgg4oaK8D4mAfSaoSmbx4","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"kind":"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","criteria":[{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/source-faithfulness@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"I compared every statement and every target changeInstruction with the complete 6120-byte source and with the admitted Intent (9f9c337f), Product (0f5e3bf0) and Requirements (7a978d3c) assets. The worksite copy of the source has digest c799b9e4…, which matches the member. Every sourceQuote in the candidate is an exact, unique substring of that member.\n\nThe design carries every source instruction faithfully:\n- the eight surfaces at exactly the source paths;\n- the conformance pressure, the seven named surfaces and the verbatim ABG sentence;\n- the implementation design's authority line, the minimal helloWorld module and the named surfaces, including 'execution result';\n- private:true and type:module;\n- both test-design obligations, including 'same exported function';\n- node:test and node:assert/strict, the exact import and a strict assertion in both verifiers;\n- the plan's exact command and args, a pass count of 2 (the source says at least 2), 'fail 0' and assertedReturnValue;\n- a file-less result;\n- the conjunctive acceptance rule and the TAP-glyph tolerance, which never excuses a failure.\n\nThe two inaccuracies I found in the previous assessment are fixed. Statement 01 no longer lists execution-evidence/ as existing; the pre-construction root holds only .abiogenesis, the source copy and semantic-assets. Statement 08 no longer asserts that the ABI owns module_export_return_exact.\n\nNew content is labelled as design, not source law:\n- rule D-suite;\n- the proposed planSatisfied definition (req-pressure:04);\n- the test-design clause (4) on single tests with no skip, todo, only, describe or it (design-pressure:08).\n\nI checked the prescribed file bodies against every checker specification. single-test, verifiers-total-tests, name-prefix, no-other-test-forms, no-skip-or-focus, import-set, plan-no-pass-pin, plan-pass-floor-matches-predicate, and all edge and fact checks in check-derivation hold on the given text. The design is therefore internally consistent.\n\nI confirmed that semantic-assets/stage-2.json (sha256:bb93b54a…) presents historicalAssets/2, which is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, so design-pressure:07 is accurate.\n\nThe source's authority relations still reduce to naming and consistency checks, but the design exposes this as a gap rather than hiding it. One minor non-material point: statement 14 refers to 'G1–G3', but only G1 and G2 are labelled; the third gap is design-pressure:03.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Name package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result as separate lifecycle surfaces."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The UAT test must validate the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:03-governing-documents","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/modality-and-conflicts@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Conflicts are kept, not decided.\n- Statement 12 is labelled conflicting. It does not reproduce the per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit or the parityRule. It leaves executeFromPlan's intended meaning unruled and claims no legacy traversal parity.\n- design-pressure:10 carries all eleven open owner rulings as conflicting.\n- Choices that exceed the source are marked unassessed and repriceable (design-pressure:08), and so is verifier strength (design-pressure:09).\n- The conditional ban on pinning a pass-count fragment is kept as a conservative design choice, and 'fail 0' stays an example with the reporter unobserved.\n- planSatisfied is explicitly a proposal under req-pressure:04.\n- Acceptance stays an owner ruling.\n\nD-suite is presented as a derivation whose admission is unassessed and which leaves per-suite attribution blocked, not as satisfying the requirement.\n\nOne nuance does not change the verdict. The admitted requirement says suite passes shall be identified from an admitted observation of each suite, 'not inferred from an aggregate count'. D-suite is partly such an inference. Admission alone therefore cannot close it; that would need an owner repricing or a new per-file ABI observation. The candidate does not claim otherwise, and this assessment records it as pressure.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"executeFromPlan: false"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:12-stage-vector-conflict","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/obligation-conservation@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Coverage holds. I checked all 14 targets:\n- every bindingVersionRef equals the active version of the obligations that target lists;\n- each of the 15 active obligations has at least one implementation target and one verifier target (for example 0: src/hello.mjs plus both verifiers; 9: the plan plus check-plan and check-derivation; 14: src/hello.mjs and the plan plus check-plan).\n\nThe two defects that falsified 75ddeb06 are repaired.\n\n(1) The stdout-fragment comparison and same-run per-suite attribution are no longer deferred to the non-executing Evidence stage. They are recorded as blocking ABI gaps G1 and G2 (design-pressure:01 and 02) at requirements 88958828, 31fcd681, d8d16690, 6cec93b4, 2ac1b260 and 221df643. The candidate explicitly forbids the Evidence stage from substituting its own reading of stdout, and forbids any local parser or wrapper. That is option (b) from the previous assessment, and it is lawful under REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-008 and REQ-GLC-ABG-REQUIREMENTS-ALGEBRA-CONSUMPTION-012. Option (a), the F_D evaluator artifact that binding 0556dad6 names, is not reachable lawfully here:\n- the source fixes the planned args, so no reporter flag can be added;\n- the capability fixes environment {}, so NODE_OPTIONS cannot be used;\n- a subject script that spawns or parses the run would be an execution wrapper.\nThe obligation is therefore conserved as blocked, not weakened.\n\n(2) The unreachable construction-basis clause is now declared at every affected obligation: 5, 6, 9 and 12 (design-pressure:03, requirements 3e902569, d3d8ed21, 88958828, 9a46a129). check-derivation checks the named edges and emits 'construction-basis-not-admitted' notes rather than claiming the basis.\n\nreq-pressure:23 (whether run records and typed observations are admitted as realization) is now carried in design-pressure:04. Statement 13 lists the realization, verifier_execution and missing computation for obligations 10, 11 and 14 without merging roles. No binding is closed by a name, count or exit status.\n\nOne residual is not fully explicit. The required content for obligation 10 includes the digests of the subject surfaces that the run consumed, and the design relies on the ABI command record for these. That dependency is covered only by the general readiness pressure.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The command must be node with args"}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/bounded-claim@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Statement 16 claims a design candidate only. It says nothing has been constructed, run or observed, readiness is not fulfillment, several edges are blocked, and application coverage stays non-closing. The pre-construction observation agrees: it contains only .abiogenesis/, the source copy and semantic-assets (the rubric and stage-0, stage-1 and stage-2), and no subject surface.\n\ndependencyDisposition 'sufficient' is scoped to construction readiness only (statement 14). The construction instructions carry complete content, so the stale stage-2.json is not a construction input.\n\nThe previous overstatement in statement 08 is withdrawn, and ABI ownership of the typed observation is left unclassified. Readiness of the consumed ABI paths is explicitly not classified. The plan holds no result fields, no success is prewritten, and no acceptance, release or closure is claimed.\n\nStatement 15 identifies the revision cause correctly. The selected obligations (5, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12) match the falsified assessment whose cCall cd576c71 is the revision cause.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation","design-statement:16-stage-claim-boundary"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/executable-proof@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"The design stays within bounds:\n- All 9 commands use the admitted executable /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node, with environment {} and cwd '.'.\n- Timeouts are at most 120000 ms and grace is at most 1000 ms. The budget is 3×31000 + 6×16000 = 189000 ms; adding the 5000 ms allowance gives 194000 ms, below both 300000 and 900000. There are no HTTP launches.\n- There are 14 targets (limit 64) and 9 commands (limit 32). Paths are relative, non-traversing and unique under write root '.'.\n- dependencyPaths names only the existing source copy (digest c799b9e4…), which is under read root '.' and is not a target, so the writable targets are not widened.\n- Every predicate references a declared commandId or a target path.\n\nThe proof content is sound:\n- planned-verifier-run is exactly the source command;\n- both verifiers import the real module;\n- module_export_return_exact is the single typed-observation predicate;\n- the checkers are read-only, never spawn processes and report digests;\n- the static facts behind D-suite (exactly one test per file, two in total, no skip, todo, only, describe or it) hold on the prescribed bodies.\n\nD-suite is logically sound for node --test: exit 0, a pass count of at least 2, and two unskipped single-test files together entail that both tests passed. It is correctly kept non-closing.\n\nThe acceptance-related coverage that is still missing (the fragment comparison, same-run per-suite attribution and the construction basis) is declared as upstream or lifecycle gaps at the owning obligations, with no local compensation. That is the lawful disposition when the capability is absent.\n\nThese are preserved as prerequisites, not proof:\n- whether test_pass_count parses Node 24.7.0 output and records the observed count;\n- which reporter runs under capture;\n- whether module_export_return_exact is the F_P observation.\n\nG1 and G2 rest on the author's account of the C2 predicate set, which this assessment could not inspect.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The command must be node with args"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction"]}],"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:01-abi-gap-classification-unverified","text":"G1 and G2 depend on the author's statement that the consumed C2 predicate set has no stdout-substring predicate and no per-file attribution within one run. This assessment could not inspect that catalog.\n- If such a predicate is ready, a revised design must consume it.\n- If it is not, the gaps stay blocking at the ABI owner.\n\nREQ-GLC-ABG-REQUIREMENTS-ALGEBRA-CONSUMPTION-001 and -013 require a readiness state (ready, missing, placeholder, test_only, unwired or unpinned) for each consumed capability before ratification. None is yet recorded for per-command admission, for test_pass_count parsing and recording of the observed count, or for module_export_return_exact as the F_P observation.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/db07c18d91f1dcee127290132e58619874224e0edc21af9af0b29245818242ff"],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:02-d-suite-cannot-close-by-admission","text":"D-suite derives each suite's pass from the aggregate exit status and pass count plus static file structure. The admitted requirement forbids inferring suite passes from an aggregate count. Same-run per-suite attribution therefore closes only through one of two routes: a per-file observation supplied by the ABI owner, or an owner ruling that reprices the attribution clause. Admitting D-suite alone is not enough. component-suite-run and uat-suite-run remain corroboration from separate runs.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/6cec93b453f2df9b331e5908febb36e581998805218c49fab406ce4e9370a287","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/2ac1b260a4c172edf2c948ed18390b42302657bec15407901409728e5e2e5ad3","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/221df643ebe7e2b283bc56db2ae7e674def6ca0cdc88ba89c7b0e645ea40dd71"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:03-construction-basis-lifecycle-gap","text":"The digest-basis clause stays unprovable for obligations 5, 6, 9 and 12 while construction happens in one activation. Closure needs one of two things: staged construction activations through lawful re-entry, with predecessors as declared read paths, or an owner ruling that reprices the clause. check-derivation proves only named edges and cross-surface consistency.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/3e9025692e1fd4b454ea40c9695fa2b37c662812a79169a50099d8fd1ab54210","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d3d8ed21b5d15af3a3a3bf1ccd3ff5adf06b9e202ca112bfbbc7195c5d0d54ba","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/9a46a12976a1020d5ab1e12524f47719058ff6b9e5bb78fff621d8f120938321"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:04-run-record-content","text":"The required content for obligation 10 includes the working directory, stdout and stderr digests, and the digests of the subject surfaces the planned run consumed. The design relies on the ABI command record for all of these. It shows no specific binding of consumed-surface digests to planned-verifier-run; this is covered only by the general readiness pressure in design-pressure:04.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:05-stale-requirements-materialization","text":"semantic-assets/stage-2.json on disk is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, and no admitted copy of 7a978d3c exists on disk. Construction does not depend on it, but assessment and any future re-entry must use the admitted asset. The correction belongs to the runtime or lifecycle owner.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:06-carried-rulings-and-unobserved-runtime","text":"The owner rulings carried in design-pressure:10 remain open, and this assessment grants none. Also still unobserved:\n- the Node 24.7.0 reporter format under capture;\n- whether 'fail 0' and the 'component:' and 'uat:' test names appear in the admitted stdout;\n- whether either verifier fails on a wrong greeting.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:07-application-unrealized","text":"Every application obligation remains unrealized:\n- no surface, admitted run or typed observation exists;\n- no Evidence binding, semantic assessment or owner acceptance exists.\n\nThe acceptance edge stays blocked until G1 and G2 are resolved at their owner. Application coverage stays non-closing.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362222,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362222},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f413b77d-1b94-4180-8acc-38e0c5e04077","uuid":"2d2ddfd5-c218-4641-a5ad-174dd070bb10","timestamp":"2026-09-26T08:14:09.499Z","request_id":"req_011CfRi7un9tGKRuXJT96oR5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JLgg4oaK8D4mAfSaoSmbx4":{"kind":"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","criteria":[{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/source-faithfulness@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"I compared every statement and every target changeInstruction with the complete 6120-byte source and with the admitted Intent (9f9c337f), Product (0f5e3bf0) and Requirements (7a978d3c) assets. The worksite copy of the source has digest c799b9e4…, which matches the member. Every sourceQuote in the candidate is an exact, unique substring of that member.\n\nThe design carries every source instruction faithfully:\n- the eight surfaces at exactly the source paths;\n- the conformance pressure, the seven named surfaces and the verbatim ABG sentence;\n- the implementation design's authority line, the minimal helloWorld module and the named surfaces, including 'execution result';\n- private:true and type:module;\n- both test-design obligations, including 'same exported function';\n- node:test and node:assert/strict, the exact import and a strict assertion in both verifiers;\n- the plan's exact command and args, a pass count of 2 (the source says at least 2), 'fail 0' and assertedReturnValue;\n- a file-less result;\n- the conjunctive acceptance rule and the TAP-glyph tolerance, which never excuses a failure.\n\nThe two inaccuracies I found in the previous assessment are fixed. Statement 01 no longer lists execution-evidence/ as existing; the pre-construction root holds only .abiogenesis, the source copy and semantic-assets. Statement 08 no longer asserts that the ABI owns module_export_return_exact.\n\nNew content is labelled as design, not source law:\n- rule D-suite;\n- the proposed planSatisfied definition (req-pressure:04);\n- the test-design clause (4) on single tests with no skip, todo, only, describe or it (design-pressure:08).\n\nI checked the prescribed file bodies against every checker specification. single-test, verifiers-total-tests, name-prefix, no-other-test-forms, no-skip-or-focus, import-set, plan-no-pass-pin, plan-pass-floor-matches-predicate, and all edge and fact checks in check-derivation hold on the given text. The design is therefore internally consistent.\n\nI confirmed that semantic-assets/stage-2.json (sha256:bb93b54a…) presents historicalAssets/2, which is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, so design-pressure:07 is accurate.\n\nThe source's authority relations still reduce to naming and consistency checks, but the design exposes this as a gap rather than hiding it. One minor non-material point: statement 14 refers to 'G1–G3', but only G1 and G2 are labelled; the third gap is design-pressure:03.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Name package.json, src/hello.mjs, design/test-design.md, test/component/hello.test.mjs, test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, test-execution-plan.json, and execution result as separate lifecycle surfaces."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"State that ABG owns startup admission, registry selection, graph-call opening, vector traversal, F_P dispatch, evidence admission, event emission, closure, and convergence."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The UAT test must validate the user-visible greeting contract through the same exported function."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:03-governing-documents","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/modality-and-conflicts@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Conflicts are kept, not decided.\n- Statement 12 is labelled conflicting. It does not reproduce the per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit or the parityRule. It leaves executeFromPlan's intended meaning unruled and claims no legacy traversal parity.\n- design-pressure:10 carries all eleven open owner rulings as conflicting.\n- Choices that exceed the source are marked unassessed and repriceable (design-pressure:08), and so is verifier strength (design-pressure:09).\n- The conditional ban on pinning a pass-count fragment is kept as a conservative design choice, and 'fail 0' stays an example with the reporter unobserved.\n- planSatisfied is explicitly a proposal under req-pressure:04.\n- Acceptance stays an owner ruling.\n\nD-suite is presented as a derivation whose admission is unassessed and which leaves per-suite attribution blocked, not as satisfying the requirement.\n\nOne nuance does not change the verdict. The admitted requirement says suite passes shall be identified from an admitted observation of each suite, 'not inferred from an aggregate count'. D-suite is partly such an inference. Admission alone therefore cannot close it; that would need an owner repricing or a new per-file ABI observation. The candidate does not claim otherwise, and this assessment records it as pressure.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"executeFromPlan: false"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedStdoutMatch must include stable zero-failure evidence such as fail 0"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:02-implementation-realization","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:12-stage-vector-conflict","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/obligation-conservation@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Coverage holds. I checked all 14 targets:\n- every bindingVersionRef equals the active version of the obligations that target lists;\n- each of the 15 active obligations has at least one implementation target and one verifier target (for example 0: src/hello.mjs plus both verifiers; 9: the plan plus check-plan and check-derivation; 14: src/hello.mjs and the plan plus check-plan).\n\nThe two defects that falsified 75ddeb06 are repaired.\n\n(1) The stdout-fragment comparison and same-run per-suite attribution are no longer deferred to the non-executing Evidence stage. They are recorded as blocking ABI gaps G1 and G2 (design-pressure:01 and 02) at requirements 88958828, 31fcd681, d8d16690, 6cec93b4, 2ac1b260 and 221df643. The candidate explicitly forbids the Evidence stage from substituting its own reading of stdout, and forbids any local parser or wrapper. That is option (b) from the previous assessment, and it is lawful under REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-008 and REQ-GLC-ABG-REQUIREMENTS-ALGEBRA-CONSUMPTION-012. Option (a), the F_D evaluator artifact that binding 0556dad6 names, is not reachable lawfully here:\n- the source fixes the planned args, so no reporter flag can be added;\n- the capability fixes environment {}, so NODE_OPTIONS cannot be used;\n- a subject script that spawns or parses the run would be an execution wrapper.\nThe obligation is therefore conserved as blocked, not weakened.\n\n(2) The unreachable construction-basis clause is now declared at every affected obligation: 5, 6, 9 and 12 (design-pressure:03, requirements 3e902569, d3d8ed21, 88958828, 9a46a129). check-derivation checks the named edges and emits 'construction-basis-not-admitted' notes rather than claiming the basis.\n\nreq-pressure:23 (whether run records and typed observations are admitted as realization) is now carried in design-pressure:04. Statement 13 lists the realization, verifier_execution and missing computation for obligations 10, 11 and 14 without merging roles. No binding is closed by a name, count or exit status.\n\nOne residual is not fully explicit. The required content for obligation 10 includes the digests of the subject surfaces that the run consumed, and the design relies on the ABI command record for these. That dependency is covered only by the general readiness pressure.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior component_test_source and uat_test_source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The command must be node with args"}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction","design-statement:13-proof-role-mapping","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/bounded-claim@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Statement 16 claims a design candidate only. It says nothing has been constructed, run or observed, readiness is not fulfillment, several edges are blocked, and application coverage stays non-closing. The pre-construction observation agrees: it contains only .abiogenesis/, the source copy and semantic-assets (the rubric and stage-0, stage-1 and stage-2), and no subject surface.\n\ndependencyDisposition 'sufficient' is scoped to construction readiness only (statement 14). The construction instructions carry complete content, so the stale stage-2.json is not a construction input.\n\nThe previous overstatement in statement 08 is withdrawn, and ABI ownership of the typed observation is left unclassified. Readiness of the consumed ABI paths is explicitly not classified. The plan holds no result fields, no success is prewritten, and no acceptance, release or closure is claimed.\n\nStatement 15 identifies the revision cause correctly. The selected obligations (5, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12) match the falsified assessment whose cCall cd576c71 is the revision cause.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:14-dependencies-and-readiness","design-statement:15-revision-reconciliation","design-statement:16-stage-claim-boundary"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/design/executable-proof@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"The design stays within bounds:\n- All 9 commands use the admitted executable /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/24.7.0/bin/node, with environment {} and cwd '.'.\n- Timeouts are at most 120000 ms and grace is at most 1000 ms. The budget is 3×31000 + 6×16000 = 189000 ms; adding the 5000 ms allowance gives 194000 ms, below both 300000 and 900000. There are no HTTP launches.\n- There are 14 targets (limit 64) and 9 commands (limit 32). Paths are relative, non-traversing and unique under write root '.'.\n- dependencyPaths names only the existing source copy (digest c799b9e4…), which is under read root '.' and is not a target, so the writable targets are not widened.\n- Every predicate references a declared commandId or a target path.\n\nThe proof content is sound:\n- planned-verifier-run is exactly the source command;\n- both verifiers import the real module;\n- module_export_return_exact is the single typed-observation predicate;\n- the checkers are read-only, never spawn processes and report digests;\n- the static facts behind D-suite (exactly one test per file, two in total, no skip, todo, only, describe or it) hold on the prescribed bodies.\n\nD-suite is logically sound for node --test: exit 0, a pass count of at least 2, and two unskipped single-test files together entail that both tests passed. It is correctly kept non-closing.\n\nThe acceptance-related coverage that is still missing (the fragment comparison, same-run per-suite attribution and the construction basis) is declared as upstream or lifecycle gaps at the owning obligations, with no local compensation. That is the lawful disposition when the capability is absent.\n\nThese are preserved as prerequisites, not proof:\n- whether test_pass_count parses Node 24.7.0 output and records the observed count;\n- which reporter runs under capture;\n- whether module_export_return_exact is the F_P observation.\n\nG1 and G2 rest on the author's account of the C2 predicate set, which this assessment could not inspect.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"The command must be node with args"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."}],"statementRefs":["design-statement:01-subject-topology","design-statement:04-verifiers","design-statement:05-execution-plan","design-statement:06-native-execution","design-statement:07-acceptance-computation","design-statement:08-typed-outcome-observation","design-statement:09-checker-verifiers","design-statement:10-derivation-direction"]}],"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:01-abi-gap-classification-unverified","text":"G1 and G2 depend on the author's statement that the consumed C2 predicate set has no stdout-substring predicate and no per-file attribution within one run. This assessment could not inspect that catalog.\n- If such a predicate is ready, a revised design must consume it.\n- If it is not, the gaps stay blocking at the ABI owner.\n\nREQ-GLC-ABG-REQUIREMENTS-ALGEBRA-CONSUMPTION-001 and -013 require a readiness state (ready, missing, placeholder, test_only, unwired or unpinned) for each consumed capability before ratification. None is yet recorded for per-command admission, for test_pass_count parsing and recording of the observed count, or for module_export_return_exact as the F_P observation.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/db07c18d91f1dcee127290132e58619874224e0edc21af9af0b29245818242ff"],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:02-d-suite-cannot-close-by-admission","text":"D-suite derives each suite's pass from the aggregate exit status and pass count plus static file structure. The admitted requirement forbids inferring suite passes from an aggregate count. Same-run per-suite attribution therefore closes only through one of two routes: a per-file observation supplied by the ABI owner, or an owner ruling that reprices the attribution clause. Admitting D-suite alone is not enough. component-suite-run and uat-suite-run remain corroboration from separate runs.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d8d166906884606b13f9a636db2c1efd2c9718e4c7984b671b0c92df67d5ebe9","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/6cec93b453f2df9b331e5908febb36e581998805218c49fab406ce4e9370a287","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/2ac1b260a4c172edf2c948ed18390b42302657bec15407901409728e5e2e5ad3","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/221df643ebe7e2b283bc56db2ae7e674def6ca0cdc88ba89c7b0e645ea40dd71"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:03-construction-basis-lifecycle-gap","text":"The digest-basis clause stays unprovable for obligations 5, 6, 9 and 12 while construction happens in one activation. Closure needs one of two things: staged construction activations through lawful re-entry, with predecessors as declared read paths, or an owner ruling that reprices the clause. check-derivation proves only named edges and cross-surface consistency.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/3e9025692e1fd4b454ea40c9695fa2b37c662812a79169a50099d8fd1ab54210","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/d3d8ed21b5d15af3a3a3bf1ccd3ff5adf06b9e202ca112bfbbc7195c5d0d54ba","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/88958828d9af4ca553462c38b29d8514f35242708d8a0492cca59db11f457ed0","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/9a46a12976a1020d5ab1e12524f47719058ff6b9e5bb78fff621d8f120938321"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:04-run-record-content","text":"The required content for obligation 10 includes the working directory, stdout and stderr digests, and the digests of the subject surfaces the planned run consumed. The design relies on the ABI command record for all of these. It shows no specific binding of consumed-surface digests to planned-verifier-run; this is covered only by the general readiness pressure in design-pressure:04.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/31fcd6813562347ff58ee3be2eed9320788c8a8ea87ec9d16a71e1fb994dae55"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:05-stale-requirements-materialization","text":"semantic-assets/stage-2.json on disk is the falsified Requirements candidate cef9896f, and no admitted copy of 7a978d3c exists on disk. Construction does not depend on it, but assessment and any future re-entry must use the admitted asset. The correction belongs to the runtime or lifecycle owner.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:06-carried-rulings-and-unobserved-runtime","text":"The owner rulings carried in design-pressure:10 remain open, and this assessment grants none. Also still unobserved:\n- the Node 24.7.0 reporter format under capture;\n- whether 'fail 0' and the 'component:' and 'uat:' test names appear in the admitted stdout;\n- whether either verifier fails on a wrong greeting.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:07-application-unrealized","text":"Every application obligation remains unrealized:\n- no surface, admitted run or typed observation exists;\n- no Evidence binding, semantic assessment or owner acceptance exists.\n\nThe acceptance edge stays blocked until G1 and G2 are resolved at their owner. Application coverage stays non-closing.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"}]}}}
